        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\triangle BCD\\sim\\triangle ACB$ (AAA).",
          "worked": "Angle BCD equals ACB because D lies on AC. Also $\\angle BDC=90°=\\angle ABC$. Therefore the remaining angle CBD equals CAB, giving $\\triangle BCD\\sim\\triangle ACB$ by AAA with B→A,C→C,D→B.",
